{# enforcement/templates/punchlist.md.tera — uses sahjhan v0.6.1 render context
   Uses where_eq filter for cleaner event filtering. #}
# Punchlist

**Protocol:** {{ protocol.name }} v{{ protocol.version }}
**Run:** {{ template_instance_id | default(value="?") }}
**State:** {{ state.label }}
**Ledger:** {{ ledger_len }} events

Open findings only. Resolved and deferred rows are in `PUNCHLIST-ARCHIVE.md`.

{# One row per finding id. A finding filed twice under one id — a correction
   re-recorded without retracting the original — otherwise renders as two
   rows, and every count taken off this file is wrong by the difference.
   unique_by keeps the last, so the correction supersedes what it corrects.

   Closed rows go to the archive rather than being dropped: recon's cold-file
   coverage scan reads archived punchlists to decide which files a prior run
   ever looked at, and a converged run has no open findings at all. #}
{% set findings = events | where_eq(attribute="event_type", value="finding") | unique_by(attribute="fields.id") -%}
{% set resolved_ids = events | where_eq(attribute="event_type", value="finding_resolved") | unique_by(attribute="fields.id") | map(attribute="fields.id") -%}
{% set deferred_ids = events | where_eq(attribute="event_type", value="finding_deferred") | unique_by(attribute="fields.id") | map(attribute="fields.id") -%}

{# One line per open finding: id, severity, file:line, and a summary capped at
   12 words. The six-column form carried `category` and `perspective` on every
   row — neither is branched on in the fix loop — and the whole description,
   which is what made this file 81k tokens against ~10-12k for the four fields
   below. 23% of every load was already-resolved rows before the archive split.

   The summary is the description truncated here, not a second field the agent
   writes: two texts for one fact drift, and the ledger keeps the full prose
   for `findings.py show`. Splitting on a single space means runs of
   whitespace produce empty tokens, so the cap is at most 12 words and
   sometimes fewer — never more, which is the direction that matters. #}
| ID | Severity | Location | Summary |
|----|----------|----------|---------|
{% for severity in ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"] -%}
{% set sev_findings = findings | where_eq(attribute="fields.severity", value=severity) -%}
{% for e in sev_findings -%}
{% if resolved_ids is not containing(e.fields.id) and deferred_ids is not containing(e.fields.id) -%}
| {{ e.fields.id }} | {{ severity }} | {{ e.fields.location | replace(from="|", to="\|") }} | {{ e.fields.description | replace(from="|", to="\|") | replace(from="
", to=" ") | split(pat=" ") | slice(end=12) | join(sep=" ") }} |
{% endif -%}
{% endfor -%}
{% endfor %}
